# IYDT-GSRP input data

These CSV files support the seismic, acoustic, optical, and crater analyses
under `../../../Runfiles/IYDT-gsrp`. The seismic, acoustic, and optical data
were provided by Sean Ford of Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory. The
repository publications and user manual provide scientific provenance and
units.

## Files

| File | Rows | Role | Principal columns |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `seismic_cal.csv` | 392 | benchmark calibration | `Y1`, `Y2`, source/path/station identifiers, type, log range, yield, C2N, HOB |
| `seismic_new.csv` | 3 | SUGAR new event | same seismic responses and covariates, without C2N |
| `acoustic_cal.csv` | 411 | benchmark calibration | `Y1`, `Y2`, source/path/station identifiers, type, scaled temperature/pressure, log range, yield, C2N, HOB |
| `acoustic_new.csv` | 5 | SUGAR new event | acoustic responses and covariates, without C2N |
| `optical_cal.csv` | 25 | benchmark calibration | `Y1`, `Y2`, source, scaled temperature/pressure, yield, HOB |
| `optical_new.csv` | 1 | SUGAR new event | optical responses and covariates |
| `crater_cal.csv` | 6 | benchmark calibration | `Y1`, `Y2`, source, yield, HOB |
| `crater_new.csv` | 1 | SUGAR new event | crater responses and covariates |

Counts exclude the header row. `W` is log-yield in the supplied decks;
`lRange`, `logTempSc`, and `logPressureSc` are already transformed inputs.
Do not apply a second transformation when using the canonical forward models.

## Use and maintenance

Run decks refer to these files by basename beneath their configured data root.
Treat them as immutable inputs. If a dataset changes:

1. retain the exact header names expected by preprocessing and application
   code;
2. review every IYDT deck that references the file;
3. rerun `Test-Docker` suites `IYDT/Seismic`, `IYDT/Acoustic`,
   `IYDT/Optical`, and `IYDT/Crater`; and
4. create new Docker analysis jobs so their input snapshots include the change.

Generated workspaces, optimization files, logs, and plots do not belong in this
directory.
